ared with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Its stored properties","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are its properties, so a misspelled or mistyped one is a compile error. Its type gives the name","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destinations record it under, the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory","type":"reference"},{"text":" whose consent decides whether it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered, and the version of its shape. Each has a default: the type’s name,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory\/analytics","type":"reference"},{"text":" and 1.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two property types carry rules of their own. A "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" value, such as an email address,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"prints as "},{"code":"<redacted>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and has no public accessor: a destination reads it through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventRecord\/reveal(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", which gives "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" once a delivery has redacted the record. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Refined","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" value satisfies every "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Constraint","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" its "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Refinement","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","tex